DATASET_TITLE Braking: Fade Test, Repeated 0-100-0 km/h
#RingCtrl8 1
#RingCtrl9 1

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example demsonstrates modeling a brake fade test in CarSim using Events.
#
#The vehicle makes repeated 0-100-0 km/h runs. The vehicle position is reset to zero station position for the beginning of each test cycle.
#
#You can see in the plots that the brake rotors must reach their ideal operating temperature before they can generate enough brake torque to drive the wheels below their ABS slip target, thus engaging the ABS. This happens for stops 3, 4, 5, and 6. As the rotor temperatures increase beyond their operating range the amount of brake torque they can generate decreases, preventing the brakes from driving the wheels below their ABS slip target. This is equivalent to brake pad fade and when this happens, the ABS does not engage. This effect may be seen in the plots for Brake Torque and Long. Accel. of CG's.
#
#Also shown is the animation of the brake rotors glowing from the heat.
#
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: CarSim Run Control; { Brake Tests } Braking: Fade Test, Repeated 0-100-0 km/h
